{"type":"text","timestamp":1794545980982,"sessionID":"ses_e2cbe0f67ffeARtW3ynN5Ce39R","part":{"id":"prt_1d3468ca4002DmXPygVvL3Gk7t","sessionID":"ses_e2cbe0f67ffeARtW3ynN5Ce39R","messageID":"msg_1d34675d3001nr8VvpcZHzW3hV","type":"text","text":"T009 complete. Here is the report.\n\n**Files written**\n\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs`\n  - Added `CLAUDE_POINTER_PATH = 'CLAUDE.md'`.\n  - Built `claudePointer` as `` `@${manifest.root_file}\\n` `` in `compose()`.\n  - The removed-copies loop now writes `{ action: 'replace', content: claudePointer }` for `CLAUDE.md`, and still `remove` for every other folded copy. `removedCopies` is untouched, so the survival proof still checks folded lines.\n  - Immediately before `composition.writes`, a `CLAUDE.md` create is added when any file entry is `create`/`replace`/`remove` and `CLAUDE.md` neither exists nor is a symlink.\n  - Updated the `--remove-claude-md` usage line to `fold it and leave an @AGENTS.md pointer in its place (the default)`.\n  - Added the comment: Claude Code reads only `CLAUDE.md`, so the pointer is its one route to the root document.\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/agents-md-embed.test.cjs`\n  - Changed the two named assertions at lines 638 and 842 to expect `@AGENTS.md\\n`.\n  - Added the case `an adopted tree with no CLAUDE.md gains the pointer`.\n\n**Verify output**\n\n```\n$ node --test .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/agents-md-embed.test.cjs\n...\n✔ claude-only creates the root document and removes the copy (409.536708ms)\n✔ --keep-claude-md keeps the copy it folded (344.446625ms)\n✔ an adopted tree with no CLAUDE.md gains the pointer (364.0945ms)\n...\nℹ tests 36\nℹ pass 36\nℹ fail 0\n```\n\n```\n$ git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff -U0 HEAD -- .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/agents-md-embed.test.cjs | rg -c \"^-\\s+assert\"\n2\n```\n\n```\n$ rg -n \"keepClaudeMd\" .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs\n148:    keepClaudeMd: false,\n171:    } else if (argument === '--keep-claude-md') options.keepClaudeMd = true;\n172:    else if (argument === '--remove-claude-md') options.keepClaudeMd = false;\n639: * @param {{root: string, manifest: Object, keepClaudeMd?: boolean, createRouter?: boolean}} input\n642:function compose({ root, manifest, keepClaudeMd = false, createRouter = false }) {\n748:    if (copy.path === 'CLAUDE.md' && keepClaudeMd) {\n1249:  const composition = compose({ root: options.root, manifest, keepClaudeMd: options.keepClaudeMd, createRouter: options.createRouter });\n1314:  const composition = compose({ root: options.root, manifest, keepClaudeMd: options.keepClaudeMd, createRouter: options.createRouter });\n```\n\n**Not done**\n\nNothing in this task was left undone. The docs `doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml` and `agents-md.md` still describe removal, but those belong to T018 and were left alone. `tasks.md` was not ticked.","time":{"start":1794545978532,"end":1794545980982}}}
